Oxide Bloom
Ingredients: PSY / ACID ROCK & PSYCHEDELIA + CYBERPUNK & DYSTOPIAN + Electric Guitar
Creative Catalyst: Reverse-engineered from a corrupted cassette found inside a flooded, subterranean civic time capsule.

Oxide Bloom is the sound of high-decibel 1970s psychedelic heavy-jam freakouts resurrected through the corroded, glitch-bitten circuitry of a subterranean megacity. Searing, sustain-drenched electric guitar leads—slathered in vintage germanium fuzz and tape-head flutter—collide with mechanical industrial rhythms, poisoned subterranean drone textures, and low-frequency electrical hum. It is lysergic, chemically unstable acid rock performed not in sun-drenched festival meadows, but under buzzing sodium grow-lamps and dripping conduit pipes.

Genre DNA
- Tempo & Pulse: 68–92 BPM; a dragging, narcotic krautrock motorik or a heavy, half-time blues-rock stomp weighed down by mechanical friction, fluctuating wow-and-flutter, and sluggish mechanical inertia.
- Harmonic Palette: Phrygian dominant and Dorian modal vamps, microtonally bent fifths, scorched minor pentatonics, and disorienting quarter-tone tape-slurs caused by physical magnetic drag.
- Production Signatures: Extreme multi-generational cassette saturation with artificial dropouts, dual-amp bi-amping (one vintage tube stack pushed to sagging power-tube meltdown paired with an abrasive, solid-state industrial DI), and spring reverb tanks physically agitated with contact microphones.
- Dynamics: Long, hypnotic raga-like slow burns that simmer beneath choking walls of tape hiss before erupting into blinding, overdriven wah-wah freakouts that collapse abruptly into cavernous feedback loops.

Scene & Origin Lore
The movement broke out in the flooded service sub-levels beneath the New Kowloon Hydro-Plex during the rolling blackouts of the late 2040s. Salvage scavengers cracked open an unregistered 1990s municipal time capsule, pulling up an oxidized, silt-caked cassette labeled only with degraded grease pencil. When played back on a patched, motor-skewed deck, the tape's decayed acid-rock soloing and warped acoustic flutter sounded like an alien hymn to the tech-squatters. Within months, an entire counterculture of "Oxide Heads" emerged in abandoned aeroponic vaults. Fashioning garments from salt-crusted military surplus, copper-wire macramé, and welder goggles lined with strobe filters, they hold sweat-drenched, all-night "demag rituals" where modified vintage solid-body guitars are run through daisy-chained, dying cassette players to channel what they call "the warm rot."

Typical Instruments: Heavily modified electric guitars (loaded with hot P-90s, tuned down, played with slide and rusted steel rasps), reel-to-reel and cassette loop delays, cracked analog synthesizers (Korg MS-20, Roland System-100), vintage Univox Super-Fuzz and Cry Baby wah pedals, and acoustic drum kits fitted with sheet-metal dampeners.  
For Fans Of: Acid Mothers Temple, The Soft Moon, King Gizzard & The Lizard Wizard (Flying Microtonal Banana era), Earthless.

